{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.orbital_fourier_decomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.orbital_fourier_decomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.orbital_fourier_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.orbital_fourier_decomposition","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/orbital_fourier_decomposition.lean#L36-L126","doc":"**Manuscript statement** (full body):\n\n**Proposition.**\nLet $\\varrho: S^1 \\hookrightarrow \\Sigma_4$ be the trefoil\n$T_{2,3}$ embedded in the Bring's surface, and let\n$N = N_{\\varrho/\\Sigma_4}$ be the normal bundle.  The four\nquantum numbers $(n, \\ell, m, s)$ arise from the Fourier\ndecomposition of sections $\\sigma \\in \\Gamma(N)$ as follows.\n\n**The normal bundle.**\n\nThe trefoil $\\varrho(S^1)$ is a smooth closed curve in the\n$3$-dimensional Bring's surface $\\Sigma_4$ (viewed locally as a\nreal $3$-manifold via the spatial realization functor).  The\nnormal bundle $N$ is a rank-$2$ real vector bundle over\n$S^1$:\n\n$$\n  N_p =  T_p \\Sigma_4 / T_p \\varrho\n  \\qquad\\text{for } p \\in \\varrho(S^1).\n$$\n\nAt each point of the trefoil, $N_p \\cong \\mathbb{R}^2$ — two\nindependent transverse directions.  A section\n$\\sigma \\in \\Gamma(N)$ is a smooth choice of transverse\ndisplacement at each point of the trefoil.\n\n**Parametrisation.**\n\nLet $\\varTheta \\in [0, 2\\pi)$ parametrise the trefoil\n$\\varrho(\\varTheta)$.  A section decomposes as\n\n$$\n  \\sigma(\\varTheta)\n  = \n  \\sum_{\\ell=0}^{\\infty}\n  \\bigl(\n    a_\\ell \\cos(\\ell\\varTheta) + b_\\ell \\sin(\\ell\\varTheta)\n  \\bigr)\n  \\hat{n}_1(\\varTheta)\n  + \n  \\sum_{\\ell=0}^{\\infty}\n  \\bigl(\n    c_\\ell \\cos(\\ell\\varTheta) + d_\\ell \\sin(\\ell\\varTheta)\n  \\bigr)\n  \\hat{n}_2(\\varTheta)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\hat{n}_1(\\varTheta), \\hat{n}_2(\\varTheta)$ are an\northonormal frame for $N_{\\varrho(\\varTheta)}$ that rotates\nsmoothly as $\\varTheta$ varies.\n\nThe **total framing twist** is\n\n$$\n  k =  \\mathrm{tw}(\\sigma)\n  = \n  \\frac{1}{2\\pi} \\oint_{S^1}\n  \\kappa(\\sigma, \\hat{n}_1)  d\\varTheta\n$$\n\nwhere $\\kappa$ is the rotation angle of $\\sigma$ relative to\nthe Seifert framing.  The shell number is\n$n = k/2 + 1$ ([Reidemeister\ninvariance](#prop:reidemeister-mass-invariance)).\n\n**The four quantum numbers.**\n\n**(1) Principal quantum number $n$.**\n\nThe total twist $k = 2(n-1)$ is the **global R-I count** —\nthe self-linking number relative to the Seifert framing.  It\nconstrains the total energy:\n\n$$\n  E_n =  -\\frac{E_{\\mat\n\n[…truncated; see manuscript for remainder…]\n\n    The Lean encoding below *names* the residual proposition as a\n    `def … : Prop` over the manuscript context (the master identity\n    `k = 2(n−1)`, the orbital bound `ℓ < n`, the magnetic-number\n    range `−ℓ ≤ m ≤ ℓ`, and the spin dichotomy `s = ±½`).  Naming the\n    conditional conjecture is honest per §3b; an instance discharging\n    it (none here) would be the conjecture, the open state being the\n    absence of one. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:orbital-fourier-decomposition","label":"conj:orbital-fourier-decomposition","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrbitalFourierDecompositionContext.s","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrbitalFourierDecompositionContext.s","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/orbital_fourier_decomposition.lean#L34-L34","doc":"Spin quantum number `s : ±1/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrbitalFourierDecompositionContext.m","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrbitalFourierDecompositionContext.m","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/orbital_fourier_decomposition.lean#L32-L32","doc":"Magnetic quantum number `m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrbitalFourierDecompositionContext.ℓ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrbitalFourierDecompositionContext.ℓ","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/orbital_fourier_decomposition.lean#L30-L30","doc":"Azimuthal quantum number `ℓ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrbitalFourierDecompositionContext.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrbitalFourierDecompositionContext.n","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/orbital_fourier_decomposition.lean#L28-L28","doc":"Principal quantum number `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrbitalFourierDecompositionContext.k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrbitalFourierDecompositionContext.k","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/orbital_fourier_decomposition.lean#L26-L26","doc":"Total framing twist `k = tw(σ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrbitalFourierDecompositionContext.CategoricalObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrbitalFourierDecompositionContext.CategoricalObj","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/orbital_fourier_decomposition.lean#L24-L24","doc":"Categorical object / monoidal structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrbitalFourierDecompositionContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrbitalFourierDecompositionContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/orbital_fourier_decomposition.lean#L22-L22","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrbitalFourierDecompositionContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrbitalFourierDecompositionContext","kind":"class","line":17,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/orbital_fourier_decomposition.lean#L17-L34","doc":"Abstract context for the `orbital_fourier_decomposition` claim —\nthe manuscript-themed typed fields the claim ranges over.  The\nresidual `Prop` is *named* by `orbital_fourier_decomposition`\nbelow (§3b: naming a conditional conjecture is not a logical\nclaim), not faked by projecting a `claim_*` field. ","signatureChunk":0}]}